#: src/window/preferences.rs:395
msgid ""
"Connect both devices to the same Wi-Fi network and turn on Bluetooth.\n"
"\n"
"To send: open Quick Share → Receive on your Android device. Choose files or text here, then select the nearby device.\n"
"\n"
"To receive: turn on visibility in the Receive tab, share from your other device, and compare the matching code before accepting.\n"
"\n"
"Can’t connect? Disable VPNs or guest isolation. Allow UDP 5353 and the TCP port shown in Preferences through your firewall. A static port makes firewall setup easier.\n"
"\n"
"Supported: Android Quick Share and compatible LAN implementations. Wi-Fi Direct, Google accounts, contacts-only sharing, and relay transfers are unavailable."
msgstr ""

